  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2014-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "First, note that \\[x^4-51x^2+50 \\]\\[= (x^2-50)(x^2-1).\\]\n\nThe product is negative exactly when its two factors have opposite signs. Since \\(x^2-50<x^2-1\\), this requires \\(x^2-50<0<x^2-1\\). Thus \\(1<x^2<50\\), or \\(2\\le |x|\\le7\\). There are \\(6\\) positive and \\(6\\) negative integer solutions, for a total of \\(12\\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "Factor the expression as a product in \\(x^2\\)",
        "Find where the two factors have opposite signs"
      ],
